   MODIFICATIONS (per Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):

   a. src/depth_anything_3/utils/export/depth_vis.py
      Upstream writes a side-by-side [RGB | depth] JPEG per frame. This copy
      writes the depth visualisation alone, as PNG. The `simulation` stage
      blends these frames with the particle depth map and requires a
      single-panel image of matching dimensions, so the upstream two-panel
      JPEG output is not usable here.

   b. src/depth_anything_3/utils/export/npz.py
      Depth arrays are rounded to 6 decimals instead of 8, reducing the size
      of the exported point maps.

   c. Removed, as unused by this project: `app/` and `services/` (the Gradio
      demo and its HTTP service layer) and the standalone `cli.py`.

   No other files were altered. Diffing this directory against upstream
   depth-anything-3 will also surface unrelated version drift.

